WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.577
Question thirteen.

00:00:01.577 --> 00:00:08.412
Step one: macro scan. It asks minus fifty-three in eight-bit two's complement.

00:00:08.412 --> 00:00:11.653
One mark. Command words: “represent”.

00:00:11.653 --> 00:00:13.231
Step two: denoise.

00:00:13.231 --> 00:00:17.524
Useful, in yellow: minus fifty-three, eight bits.

00:00:17.524 --> 00:00:19.977
In cyan: “two's complement”.

00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:22.869
Useless: none — the stem is lean.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:24.446
Step three: draft.

00:00:24.446 --> 00:00:29.177
Plus fifty-three: zero zero one one zero one zero one.

00:00:29.177 --> 00:00:33.033
Invert: one one zero zero one zero one zero.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.888
Add one: one one zero zero one zero one one.

00:00:36.888 --> 00:00:38.378
Step four: P O E.

00:00:38.378 --> 00:00:45.825
A, zero zero one one zero one zero one: that is plus fifty-three, not inverted — cut.

00:00:45.825 --> 00:00:50.820
B, one zero one one zero one zero zero: wrong bits — cut.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:57.216
D, zero one zero zero one zero one one: sign bit zero, so positive — cut.

00:00:57.216 --> 00:01:05.890
Step five: sanity check and lock. The top bit is one, so negative, and it matches draft line three.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.256
So the correct answer is C.
